-- Travel graph (playerbots_travelnode*) corrections for 5.4.8: #787, #218 (beyond AC; the graph itself is AC's 3.3.5 data).
--
-- The MoP test server loads AC's upstream travel graph (playerbots_travelnode*.sql, AC data, 3780 nodes) and
-- stamps it 5.4.8-1 (TravelNode.cpp LoadOrGenerate). Its transport docks are WotLK positions. Checked here against
-- the 5.4.8 TaxiPathNode.dbc stops, the `transports` table, creature spawns
-- on the docks and the server's own mmaps (offline Detour A* over the mmaps).
--
-- Part A (#787): Scaffold Cars 149045 has stacked stops that share x/y. 13 walk links end on one floor, then jump to a
--   stop on another floor (783->1927: the path ends at z 880.3, then the 899.3 stop; 2099->1928: z 864.9, then 926.3).
--   The roam trip rejected those legs as "noroute leg-reversed" (#787, w35 Ancaranon). Each link is re-pointed to the
--   stop on its own floor, and the in-air jump point is dropped. 2386->1909 is deleted because 2386->1910 exists.
-- Part B (#218): Moonspray 176244 and the Feathermoon Ferry 177233 have no `transports` row on 5.4.8. They were never
--   spawned (w67 Obinic: wait-why not-found, then dock-wait-timeout after 1104 s at the Feathermoon dock). Their 4 dock
--   nodes (in the sea) are unlinked.
-- Part C (#218):
--   - The Orgrimmar zeppelin docks moved to the 4.0 towers (580-610 yd away). Menethil was rebuilt: its docks are 42-63
--     yd off (w67 Natius waited 718 s, 49 yd from the real stop). Auberdine is gone, so Elune's Blessing and The Bravery
--     dock at Rut'theran. Each node is moved to its 5.4.8 stop.
--   - Every zeppelin stop node is the zeppelin's origin, about 18 yd above its deck. The roam trip's dock checks allow
--     12 yd (kDockHeight), and its ground search for the step-off starts from the node's z. So no bot ever entered
--     DockWait at a zeppelin tower (0 "wait transport=<zeppelin>" lines in w67-w69), and an arriving rider found no
--     step-off point. The zeppelin nodes are moved down to the deck (the platform the zeppelin master stands on).
--   - The walk links of all these docks are rebuilt from the navmesh. Many old paths end under the tower (z 0.5 at
--     Grom'gol, z 41 at the Undercity Cloudkisser tower) or at the old position. Each new path ends on a land point on
--     the deck level within 25 yd of the stop. The Orgrimmar tower decks are a navmesh island on this core (4545 polys,
--     15 yd from the Orgrimmar ground component), and Rut'theran has no walk node on this navmesh. Those docks keep
--     their transport links only.
-- Undo: a backup of the playerbots_travelnode rows taken before this file restores every touched row.
